INSTRUCTIONS FOR FIRST-TIME TRADEWARS SETUP
-------------------------------------------

	If you're not currently running any version of TradeWars on your
system, you will need to execute the "tradewars.execute" script.  This will
create all necessary directories, copy all needed files and automatically
un-LHA all of the various archives required for the game.  Note that the
".lha" archives will be left in their appropriate directories even after they
have been un-compressed so that if you ever get a corrupted data file or want
to reset TradeWars, you will have the archives handy.
	Secondly, you will need to add a line to your BBSEvent0 file (NOTE: if
you run amaint and other maintenance files from some other port other than
Port 0, it is okay to add this line to that ports BBSEvent file instead of
BBSEvent0)
	You can either add the event from within CNet's CONFIG program with
these settings:

Port      : 0
Start Day : all
Start Time: 0
End Day   : all
End Time  : 0
Command   : 1 RUNREXX
Args      : pfiles:tradewars/TwNightlyMaint
Process   : Clear Line

or simply edit your "BBSEvent0" file and add the line:

      all    0       all    0       -o    1 pfiles:tradewars/TwNightlyMaint


	Next, go into CNet's editor with the WF command (doesn't matter what
file name you enter), and type:

[CTRL-Q]#0pfiles:tradewars/twnightlymaint}

and then MCI Read the message (with the .M command).  This will run the
Maintenance file once to initialize the game.  After it has finished running,
abort your message, go into your pfiles area, and add TradeWars! to your
pfiles listing as an ARexx file.

	That's it!  I hope your users enjoy the game as much as mine do...


